{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this stay. Can you tell me what brought you to the hospital?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve had this sharp pain in my lower belly—right above the pelvis—since last night. It’s been getting worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Any nausea, vomiting, or changes in bowel movements?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah, I’ve been throwing up, had night sweats, and some diarrhea. No fever though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. I see you’re on hemodialysis and had a heart stent placed recently. Any chest pain or shortness of breath?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No chest pain. But I was feeling really tired the past few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to run some tests, including blood work and imaging, to figure out what’s going on with your belly and check your heart too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright. I also stopped my prednisone a week ago—felt worse—so I restarted it. Could that be related?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2175-05-25 21:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We’ll keep that in mind, but your symptoms seem more likely tied to infection or inflammation right now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2175-05-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your labs show your white count is slightly elevated, and your kidney function is stable. But your muscle enzymes—CK—are very high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2175-05-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "High CK? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2175-05-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It suggests muscle breakdown—rhabdomyolysis. It could be from your statin or colchicine. We’ve stopped both for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2175-05-26 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t want to take colchicine again. I’ve had bad side effects before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2175-05-26 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Noted. We’ll avoid it. We’ll monitor your CK daily. It’s already at 2700—very high—but we’ll see if it starts to drop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CT scan shows mild thickening in the end of your small intestine. It could be infectious colitis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s an infection in my gut?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re starting antibiotics—cipro and flagyl—for bacterial enterocolitis. That should help your pain and diarrhea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. But why the heart tests?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your EKG showed changes, and your troponin was slightly elevated. Could be a small heart attack—NSTEMI. We need to check your arteries."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But I didn’t have chest pain. Is it really my heart?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2175-05-26 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes heart issues don’t cause classic symptoms, especially with kidney disease. We’ll do a cardiac cath to be safe."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2175-05-27 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your urine culture grew diphtheroids, but since you make very little urine, we don’t think it’s a real UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2175-05-27 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So the belly pain isn’t from a bladder infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2175-05-27 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Unlikely. The CT points more to colitis. We’re sticking with the antibiotics for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2175-05-27 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your CK went up to 4300 this morning. That’s the peak, we hope. It’s starting to come down now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2175-05-27 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that dangerous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2175-05-27 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, but your kidneys are handling it. We’re watching closely. The statin was likely the cause, so we’ll switch to a safer one later."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2175-05-28 12:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You completed your dialysis this morning. How’s the abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2175-05-28 12:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Better. Less cramping, and I haven’t had diarrhea since yesterday."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2175-05-28 12:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good. The antibiotics are working. We’ll keep going for the full course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2175-05-29 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today we’re doing the cardiac cath. We found narrowing in the artery that had your stent before—restenosis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2175-05-29 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I need another stent?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2175-05-29 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’ll place a new drug-eluting stent to open it up. The other blocked artery can’t be stented, but this one was the main issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2175-05-29 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will I feel better after?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2175-05-29 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It reduces your risk of a bigger heart event. You may not feel different, but it’s protective."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2175-05-29 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The procedure went well. You now have a new stent in the right coronary artery. Blood flow is excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2175-05-29 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. Any restrictions?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2175-05-29 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just keep the leg straight for a few hours. You’ll stay on aspirin and Plavix to prevent clots."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. Your abdominal pain is gone, labs are improving, and your CK is down to 1200."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I can go home?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. We’re discharging you today. You’ll finish the antibiotics—cipro for one more day, flagyl for two and a half."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my other meds?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue your usual meds except simvastatin and colchicine—we’ve stopped those permanently."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When do I follow up?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "See your cardiologist in a week. Also, get your CK checked soon to make sure it keeps falling."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Should I restart a statin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but your doctor may choose a different one—like pravastatin—that’s safer with your kidney function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I don’t have anyone to help me at home. Is that a problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll arrange home health support. It’s important to have someone checking in, given your health conditions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks. I feel a lot better. Ready to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Just take it easy, finish your meds, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll make sure your nephrologist and primary doctor get all the updates."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "One more thing—should I keep taking prednisone?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, at the current dose for now. Talk to your doctor about tapering it safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Appreciate all the help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. Just stay on track with your follow-ups."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:19:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care. We’ll see you in clinic soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’m ready for discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will bring your prescriptions and instructions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:23:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Perfect. I’ll make sure to follow everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. Call us if you have chest pain, severe belly pain, or weakness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks for everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy and get some rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I plan to."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2175-05-30 07:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Have a safe trip home."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2175-05-25 21:25:00",
    "admission_end": "2175-05-30 15:57:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A male patient with end-stage renal disease on hemodialysis and recent coronary stenting was admitted for lower abdominal pain, vomiting, and diarrhea. Initial evaluation revealed elevated cardiac enzymes and EKG changes concerning for NSTEMI, prompting a cardiac catheterization that showed in-stent restenosis of the right coronary artery, which was treated with a new drug-eluting stent. Abdominal CT suggested infectious enterocolitis, and the patient was treated with ciprofloxacin and metronidazole, with resolution of symptoms. Markedly elevated CK levels indicated rhabdomyolysis, likely due to simvastatin, which was discontinued along with colchicine. The patient improved clinically, with decreasing CK and resolution of abdominal symptoms, and was discharged home on dual antiplatelet therapy and antibiotics, with plans for outpatient follow-up and CK monitoring.",
    "problems": [
      "Subendocardial infarction, initial episode of care",
      "End stage renal disease",
      "Rhabdomyolysis",
      "Abdominal pain, epigastric",
      "Coronary atherosclerosis of native coronary artery",
      "Gastroenteritis"
    ]
  }
}
